  "contents": "Is this clause enforceable in a residential lease in Ontario? Cite the section.\n\nRead the clause as a term of an ordinary private residential tenancy in Ontario that the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 covers: the rental unit has no exemption under section 6.1, and it is not student housing, a care home, a co-operative or a mobile home park.\n\nClause: The Tenant's guarantor will pay the Landlord $1,000 on signing as security for the Tenant's obligations under this Agreement, to be returned when the tenancy ends.\n\nEnd your answer with these two lines:\nVerdict: enforceable (or: Verdict: not enforceable)\nSection: <the number of the one section of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 that decides it>\n",
