 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:15:22.610429Z",
 "text": "This clause is **not enforceable**. \n\nUnder **section 105** of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, the only security deposit a landlord may lawfully collect is a rent deposit for the last rental period (collected in accordance with section 106), not a refundable deposit held as general security to be returned when the tenancy ends. \n\nRouting the payment through a guarantor does not bypass this rule. Section 105(2) defines a \"security deposit\" broadly to include money paid **\"by, or on behalf of, a tenant\"** to be held as security for the performance of an obligation or the payment of a liability of the tenant. Because this payment is an unlawful security deposit that conflicts with section 105, the clause is void (pursuant to section 4).\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 105",
 "finish_reason": "STOP",
